Rename this file to  xmrig-wallet.txt  (remove the ".example")
and replace the line below with your own Monero wallet address.

Put ONLY the address on its own line, nothing else:

44AFFq5kSiGBoZ4NMDwYtN18obc8AemS33DBLWs3H7otXft3XjrpDtQGv7SqSsaBYBb98uNbr2VBBEt7f2wfn3RVGQBEP3A

On the next boot the Pi reads this file, writes the address into the miner
config, and starts mining. If the file is missing or the address is invalid,
the Pi simply does not mine.

Optional: create  xmrig-worker.txt  with a worker name (default: pi5).
